Z||000000||FieroHarry||10-11-2001||09:18 PM||||Well folks,<BR>After many futile hours of testing and trying this and trying that.....<BR>Listening to you all and 2 very close friends who are ASE Certified.......<P>Blind luck prevails!<P>During the early 70s (ouch im old) I was taught to "Never be just a parts replacer".<BR>They do nothing more than rip people off because there not real mechanics......<P>In the last 19+ years in the Navy I was taught "Always believe your indicators"......<P>So, after replacing the distributor(new),MPU,ECM and Ing. module twice.<P>Checking out each damn wire throught the HEI system and back to the ECM......<P><BR>Blah blah blah<P>Twas the coil after all, "EVEN THOUGHT BOTH MY COILS PASSED THE TESTS LISTED IN THE BOOKS",<BR>one was working while the other did not.<P>I sat down and listed everything I had tried and even though it past the test I had never actually swapped it out.......<P>Needless to say I feel cheated and abused by the "Mistress" and also lamented my ASE pals to boot...<P>Thanks a million to all your help and guidance through this mess, it made my Fiero withdrawel's easier to deal with.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<P><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||12
